      "side": 1,
      "message": "MdnsMultinetworkSocketClient is created in NsdService (even if nobody uses NSD), so this is trading allocating/freeing buffers for every packet vs. keeping 1500 bytes in memory at all times.\n\nGiven that mDNS is not used most of the time, it may not be a great tradeoff.\n\nMaybe the simplest is to have the buffer in EnqueueMdnsQueryCallable (created when it is constructed) and pass it down in sendPacket ? It\u0027s a bit ugly but without that, this change isn\u0027t a no-op change as it claims.",
